ok 345 CMP-240 a companion whose last hop never got its CLI lock sent no request on it: its diagnostic is never the MODELINV row the lock holder (the primary, on the same shared hop) wrote during that wait — a hop that ran still reads its own row (thirty-seventh run, a3 DISS-C-001)
ok 346 CMP-241 the MODELINV lookup finds this gate's row behind hundreds of other writers' rows: the scan is bounded by the primitive, not by the last 400 lines of a ledger every cheval caller appends to (thirty-seventh run, a3 DISS-C-002)
ok 347 CMP-242 a marker that records no where line is never ours to delete: an empty one (a crash between create and write, or another host's mid-write) or a legacy one leaves its directory to the sweep and refuses setup's claim; setup's own marker is written whole, by a rename (thirty-seventh run, c1a DISS-C-001)
